ic airway dilation pattern rather than recurrent infections alone", "Structural lung disease from birth: possible but airway dilation suggests a more specific pathophysiology", "Cardiopulmonary syndrome exacerbation: patient's tricuspid stenosis could contribute, but primary focus is on airway and sinus manifestations"], "alarm_features": ["Chronic multisystem symptoms (sinus + respiratory + growth concerns) since birth", "Persistent airway dilation on imaging"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis and Related Genetic Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3399395364460867, "posterior": 0.4059773342693813, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The chronic, multisystem nature of symptoms favors genetic disorders (B1) over isolated structural abnormalities (B3)."], "evidence_against": ["Normal growth and GI function slightly reduce CF likelihood but are consistent with atypical pancreatic sufficiency variants."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Congenital Cardiac and Pulmonary Syndromes with Multisystem Involvement", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.125, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The chronic, multisystem nature of symptoms favors genetic disorders (B1) over isolated structural abnormalities (B3)."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Lower Respiratory Tract Disorders with Structural Abnormalities", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.031, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Multisystem involvement (sinus, airway, cardiac) strongly favors genetic syndromes (